Subject: [PATCH 08090/11362] [outer-loop] ARC HUD-band capture for the
 object-perception A/B roster, gated by a two-corpus over-masking audit

The change_fidelity A/B recorded its own limitation: compare-time HUD masking was
disabled on every cell, so tn36's progress bar sat INSIDE the graded comparison --
which is why all six candidates scoring a perfect change_fidelity 1.0 are
unplannable bar-tickers. The A/B could not reconstruct a masked arm because
logical_hud_mask() needs a FRAME-coordinate mask the cells never recorded.

detect_hud_registers() does not: it consumes transitions and returns bands in the
same LOGICAL space as the transition grids, so the mask IS reconstructible from
the window alone. This captures those bands for all 20 roster games and, more
importantly, earns the right to use them.

THE SHARP TEST PASSES. tn36 row 1 -- the row its induced goal predicate literally
is -- is detected on the shipped defaults, changed_fraction 1.0. The explorer's
own frame-space detector independently masks the same row (61/64 cells, Jaccard
0.953), so two unrelated methods agree it is chrome.

IT IS STILL WITHHELD, and that is the headline. Over-masking is invisible and
catastrophic: a wrongly-masked band makes every engine score better while modelling
less. So bands pass a stage-1 audit (far-action decoupling, action-type decoupling,
solution-acts-in-band, mover-occupies-band, and the shipped REQ-6015 swallow guard)
and then a stage-2 SECOND corpus. On the random-action corpus tn36 row 1 shows the
same 1.0000 overlap / 60 changing -> 0 surviving signature as lf52, the documented
over-masking case. Detection succeeded; licensing failed. This does NOT deliver a
mask that fixes the tn36 degeneracy, and says so.

Results: 6 of 20 games ship a default mask (clean on BOTH corpora, 1.6% of cells
each); 2 bands excluded at stage 1 (cn04 -- the player occupies the band; lp85 --
no discriminator available); 3 withheld at stage 2 (lf52, su15, tn36). The audit
reproduces REQ-ARC-WMTE-6015's documented table to four decimals (lf52 1.0000
60->0, su15 0.7568 28->1), which is what makes its clean verdicts elsewhere mean
anything. Two independent full runs detect identical bands on all 20 games.

Detector thresholds were never touched -- the audit can only remove a band, and the
game the hypothesis most wanted is the one that got withheld. ls20 is flagged as
the one shipped mask no second detector corroborates.

adversarial_verify: 0 flagged. summarize_artifact: FRESH, 7/7 gates pass.
CPU-only, no LLM, no GPU, no induced engine executed. Nothing outside this
directory was touched.

